<|SECTION:VISUAL CONTEXT|>
{#
Appearance is NOT queried here. It comes from cached visual anchors, injected
after this prompt runs (agents/visual/style.py). Asking the LLM to re-describe
each character on every generation is what made the same character arrive as a
different person in every image, and it cost one query per character per image.
See docs/fork/visual-consistency-design.md.

The scene query itself is skipped when prompt distillation is on: the distiller
re-derives the moment from the instructions and the recent story context anyway,
so this call's answer would be paid for and then thrown away. Prompt building
was measured slower than image generation with it in.
#}
{% if agent_config("visual._distillation.enabled") %}
{% capture_context %}
The final prompt is composed downstream from richer context; keywords from this pass seed it.
{% end_capture_context %}
{% else %}
{% set queries = [] %}
{% if not instructions %}
{% set _ = queries.append({"id": "scene", "query": "What is happening in the current scene? Include details about the moment, actions, interactions between characters, and the environment.", "at_the_end": True}) %}
{% else %}
{% set _ = queries.append({"id": "scene", "query": "What is happening in the current scene? Include details about the moment, actions, interactions between characters, and the environment. Answer in the context of the following instructions: " ~ instructions, "at_the_end": True}) %}
{% endif %}
{% set results = batch_query_scene(queries, characters=scene.characters) %}

{% capture_context %}
{{ results["scene"] }}
{% end_capture_context %}
{% endif %}

